        "original_id": "42170128-d66e-5340-b3f3-bc5e1f1b3587",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Konstantin Somov, Andrey Ivanovich Somov, Alexandre Benois, Léon Bakst, Walter Nouvel, Dmitry Filosofov\n- Organizations: Hermitage Museum, Nevsky Pickwickians\n- Topics: 18th-century art, music\n\nFacts:\n- The Hermitage Museum has been open to the public since 1852.\n- Konstantin Somov was born into the family of Andrey Ivanovich Somov, a major art historian and curator at the Hermitage Museum.\n- Konstantin Somov became interested in 18th-century art and music at an early age.\n- The Nevsky Pickwickians originally included Alexandre Benois, who was effectively its leader, as well as Léon Bakst, Walter Nouvel, Dmitry Filosofov, and Konstantin Somov.",
